<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    The readability report source (spec 183, FR-019 to FR-022; B3, #2099). It bridges persistence and cluster
    membership so that neither depends on the other: it reads spec 180's schema-family declarations through
    Elsa.Persistence.Schema, and reports them through the Elsa.Cluster.Core contract, whose closure
    ArchitectureGuardTests.ClusterMembership keeps free of EF. A host composes it once, on its host container, with
    AddEfSchemaReadability, which also brings the in-process membership default.

    It takes no EF Core (#2143): Elsa.Persistence.Schema is the EF-free half of the schema-family surface, and every host
    shares it with the packages it loads, together with Elsa.Cluster.Core. So a host that carries no EF (ADR 0076), such
    as Elsa.Foundation.Host, composes this, and a module Nuplane loads with a private copy of
    Elsa.Persistence.EntityFramework still reaches the host's membership through the types both see.
  -->
  <!--
    Which package generations an in-place upgrade superseded (spec 183, FR-021, amended 2026-09-29): Nuplane's catalog of
    the active package set says what was replaced, and CShells' shell lifecycle says when the last generation that could
    still run it is gone. Their abstractions only, which both hosts that compose this share with their packages: a host
    without Nuplane or CShells takes neither runtime by composing readability, and has nothing superseded.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="CShells.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Nuplane.Loading.Abstractions" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Core\Elsa.Cluster.Core.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\InProcess\Elsa.Cluster.InProcess.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Persistence\Schema\Elsa.Persistence.Schema.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
